8. Edge Cases

Test at minimum:
- NEXT on an empty system
- TREAT on an empty system
- DISPLAY on an empty system
- WAITING on an empty system
- NEXT with exactly one patient
- TREAT when exactly one patient remains
- Adding patients after previous patients have been treated
- Multiple NEXT calls without TREAT
- Multiple DISPLAY calls without changing the queue
- Treating all patients and then performing another TREAT

9. Complexity Targets

ARRIVE: O(1)
NEXT: O(1)
TREAT: O(1)
DISPLAY: O(n)
WAITING: O(1)

10. Learning Goal

Recognize that a system where requests arrive over time and must be handled in arrival order naturally follows FIFO behavior.
